.*
.* QUIENVVAR: WRKENVVAR at either level. The driver gives each entry's
.* name and quoted value cut to their columns, with the IBM-style ">"
.* when cut (work/qsjob/src/qsh/env.rs). Option 1 goes on the add
.* entry (R27), whose name field is the class's 24 under the 26-wide
.* column.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 24'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=VALCL BASETYPE='CHAR 42'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=EVNAME CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=EVVALUE CLASS=VALCL.
:LISTDEF NAME=VARS VARS='OPT EVNAME EVVALUE'.
:KEYL NAME=ENVKEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F11 ACTION='RETURN 11'.F11=Display CCSIDs
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F16 ACTION='RETURN 16'.F16=Print list
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION='RETURN 17'.F17=Top
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION='RETURN 18'.F18=Bottom
:KEYI KEY=F22 ACTION='RETURN 22'.F22=Display entire field
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKENVJOB KEYL=ENVKEYS HELP=ENVH ENTER='RETURN 0'.Work with Environment Vars (*JOB)
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=VARS ACTLEN=1 SCROLL=YES EXTACT=YES.(No environment variables)
:LISTACT HELP='WRKENVJOB/OPTIONS' OPTION=1 ACTFOR=EXTACT ENTER='RETURN 101'.1=Add
:LISTACT HELP='WRKENVJOB/OPTIONS' OPTION=2 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 102'.2=Change
:LISTACT HELP='WRKENVJOB/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 104'.4=Remove
:LISTACT HELP='WRKENVJOB/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 105'.5=Display details
:LISTACT HELP='WRKENVJOB/OPTIONS' OPTION=6 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 106'.6=Print
:LISTCOL HELP='WRKENVJOB/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/EVNAME' VAR=EVNAME USAGE=OUTPUT MAXWIDTH=26 EXTACT=YES.Name
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/EVVALUE' VAR=EVVALUE USAGE=OUTPUT.Value
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Parameters or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKENVSYS KEYL=ENVKEYS HELP=ENVH ENTER='RETURN 0'.Work with Environment Vars (*SYS)
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=VARS ACTLEN=1 SCROLL=YES EXTACT=YES.(No environment variables)
:LISTACT HELP='WRKENVSYS/OPTIONS' OPTION=1 ACTFOR=EXTACT ENTER='RETURN 101'.1=Add
:LISTACT HELP='WRKENVSYS/OPTIONS' OPTION=2 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 102'.2=Change
:LISTACT HELP='WRKENVSYS/OPTIONS' OPTION=4 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 104'.4=Remove
:LISTACT HELP='WRKENVSYS/OPTIONS' OPTION=5 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 105'.5=Display details
:LISTACT HELP='WRKENVSYS/OPTIONS' OPTION=6 ACTFOR=LISTE ENTER='RETURN 106'.6=Print
:LISTCOL HELP='WRKENVSYS/OPT' VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT.Opt
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/EVNAME' VAR=EVNAME USAGE=OUTPUT MAXWIDTH=26 EXTACT=YES.Name
:LISTCOL HELP='FLD/EVVALUE' VAR=EVVALUE USAGE=OUTPUT.Value
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Parameters or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=ENVH.Work with Environment Variables - Help
:P.Each line is one environment variable of the job (*JOB) or of the system (*SYS). A job starts with a copy of the system's variables; changing the job's leaves the system's as they are.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=KEYSHLP.Function keys - Help
:P.F11 shows the CCSID each value is tagged with. F22 shows a whole name and value. F16 prints the list.
:EHELP.
.* Item, key and option help.
:HELP NAME='WRKENVJOB/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/EVNAME'.Name
:P.The name of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/EVVALUE'.Value
:P.The value of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKENVJOB/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Add
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to add it.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it.
:PT.4=Remove
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to remove it.
:PT.5=Display details
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display details it.
:PT.6=Print
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to print it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKENVSYS/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKENVSYS/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Add
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to add it.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it.
:PT.4=Remove
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to remove it.
:PT.5=Display details
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display details it.
:PT.6=Print
:PD.Type 6 next to an entry and press Enter to print it.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
